---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE, contactHref } from '../../lib/site';
---

<Page
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="BidRadar refunds your first paid month in full if you are not satisfied. Cancel any time."
  path="/refund/"
  heading="Refund Policy"
  intro="Short version: if BidRadar is not worth it to you in your first paid month, we give that month back."
  updated="October 28, 2026"
>
  <h2>First-month guarantee</h2>
  <p>
    If you are not satisfied during your first paid month, email <a href={contactHref}
      >{SITE.email}</a
    > before that month ends and ask for a refund. We refund the full amount of that first month. You
    do not need to give a reason.
  </p>

  <h2>How refunds are paid</h2>
  <p>
    Refunds go back to the original payment method through our payment provider, Creem. We start
    the refund within 5 business days of your request. Your bank or card issuer may take a few more
    days to show it.
  </p>

  <h2>After the first month</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel at any time and you will not be billed again. Months after the first one are not
    refunded for partial use, and your digest keeps arriving until the end of the period you paid
    for. If something went wrong on our side, such as digests not arriving, write to us and we will
    make it right.
  </p>

  <h2>Free sample</h2>
  <p>The {SITE.pricing.trialDays}-day sample is free and needs no payment details, so there is nothing to refund.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={contactHref}>{SITE.email}</a><br />
    {SITE.address.line1}, {SITE.address.line2}, {SITE.address.line3}, {SITE.address.country}
  </p>
</Page>
